# .links.ignore — the by-design dangling links `tt links check` may excuse (issue-011).
# One entry per line: `from -> target  # reason`. The reason is MANDATORY: a new dangling
# link fails CI unless recorded here, and recording it means explaining it.

# The manual sources cite .html siblings that exist only after `tt ssg` generates the manual
# (see the regenerate command at the foot of docs/manual-src/index.md).
docs/manual-src/getting-started.md -> allowlist.html  # generated into docs/generated by tt ssg
docs/manual-src/index.md -> foundations.html  # generated into docs/generated by tt ssg
docs/manual-src/index.md -> tool-selection.html  # generated into docs/generated by tt ssg
docs/manual-src/index.md -> allowlist.html  # generated into docs/generated by tt ssg
docs/manual-src/index.md -> statusline-manual.html  # generated into docs/generated by tt ssg

# The serverless-spa-seed template page cites the main.js its own build step produces
# (scala-cli package . --js -o main.js); the repo legitimately ships only the source.
skills/serverless-spa-seed/template/index.html -> main.js  # produced by the seed's scala-cli --js build
